claim.claim-text:
- a selection bias which is determined as one of:
1. a value which decreases with increasing number of hops between the network node (710) and the synchronization receiving device (800), when the number of hops is counted increasingly starting from the network node;
2. a value which increases with increasing number of hops between the network node (710) and the synchronization receiving device (800), when the number of hops is counted decreasingly starting from the network node (719) with a predetermined maximum number of hops;

transmitting synchronization signals from a network node and a wireless device;
receiving (910) predetermined wireless synchronization signals from synchronization sources including a synchronization source which derives its synchronization signal from the network node and the wireless device;
selecting (940) a synchronization source from among the synchronization sources according to a metric, and
determining or adjusting (950) the timing for transmission or reception of data according to the synchronization signal of the synchronization source selected
characterized by
determining (930) the selection metric for each of the synchronization sources based on a combination of:

- priority selection bias which is determined as one of:
1. a value which decreases with increasing number of hops between the network node (710) and the synchronization receiving device (800), when the number of hops is counted increasingly starting from the network node;
2. a value which increases with increasing number of hops between the network node (710) and the synchronization receiving device (800), when the number of hops is counted decreasingly starting from the network node (719) with a predetermined maximum number of hops;
